"""Specs for the Talmud tractates of Michael L. Rodkinson’s New Edition of the Babylonian Talmud (New York: New Talmud Publishing Company, 1896–1903), the one English translation of any length in the public domain (the Soncino Talmud of 1935–1952 is in copyright). One entry per tractate or group of tractates; each tractate is cut out of its scan once (several scans bind two or three volumes, so an entry repeating another is a bug: the tractates are cut by their own first chapter and their 'END OF TRACT' line). Merged into texts_archive.SPECS; built with build_texts.py --only=ids.

Not in the set: the tractates Rodkinson did not publish (the translation stops short of the whole Talmud), and Berakoth, Hagigah, Kiddushin and the rest which the Internet Archive scans we found do not hold. His translation is free and idiomatic and is known to miss and paraphrase; the Library’s Talmud entry (e-tal) is a short anthology.
"""
